  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a strong upward drift bias (approx +2-3 EUR) when forecasting from low-volatility or flat sentiment periods; apply a downward correction of 2.5% to the forecasted mean.",
    "When sentiment history shows recent spikes (1.00) followed by neutralization, the model fails to capture immediate volatility expansion; reduce forecast variance and lower expected peak levels by 4-6 EUR.",
    "Model systematically underestimates mean reversion speed after sharp price drops; true outcomes recover faster than predicted, requiring an upward adjustment of 1.5% on the first 3 days post-crash.",
    "Forecast horizon errors are non-linear: model predicts smooth linear growth but actual EU ETS prices exhibit high-frequency oscillations; apply a jaggedness penalty by reducing confidence in mid-horizon (days 10-20) predictions by 8%.",
    "Sentiment history with mixed positive/negative signals (-1.00 to 1.00) correlates with model over-smoothing; when sentiment variance > 0.5, reduce forecasted volatility and lower expected range width by 15%."
  ]
